---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import digitalProducts from '../data/digital-products.json';

const bookProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'power-without-the-panic');
const toolkitProduct = digitalProducts.find(p => p.id === 'solar-complete-toolkit-bundle');

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": "Band A Electricity Tariff vs Petrol Generator vs Solar: 2026 Nigeria Payback & Cost Index",
  "description": "Comprehensive economic research analyzing monthly power expenses under Band A DISCO tariffs (₦209/kWh) and petrol (₦1,395–₦1,450/L) against LiFePO4 solar payback periods in Nigeria.",
  "author": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "Ibadan Solar Hub"
  },
  "publisher": {
    "@type": "Organization",
    "name": "IbadanSolarHub",
    "url": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng"
  },
  "datePublished": "2026-09-16",
  "mainEntityOfPage": "https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Band A Electricity Tariff vs Petrol Generator vs Solar: 2026 Nigeria Payback Index"
  description="Comprehensive 2026 Nigerian power cost index. Compare Band A DISCO tariffs (₦209/kWh) and current petrol pump prices (₦1,395–₦1,450/L) against turnkey LiFePO4 solar installation payback periods."
  schema={schema}
>
  {/* Hero Header */}
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900 via-slate-800 to-slate-900 text-white py-14 md:py-20 border-b border-slate-800 relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(#f59e0b_1px,transparent_1px)] [background-size:24px_24px] opacity-10"></div>
    <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 text-center">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3.5 py-1.5 bg-solar-500/10 text-solar-400 border border-solar-500/20 rounded-full text-xs font-semibold mb-4">
        📊 2026 Nigerian Energy Economics Whitepaper
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black tracking-tight leading-tight max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        Band A Electricity Tariff vs. Petrol Generator vs. Solar: <span class="text-solar-400">The 2026 Payback Index</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-slate-300 max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-4 leading-relaxed">
        With Band A DISCO tariffs at <strong>₦209 – ₦225 per kWh</strong> and petrol pump prices now surging between <strong>₦1,395 and ₦1,450 per litre</strong>, how fast does solar actually pay for itself in Nigeria? Here is the exact mathematical payback model.
      </p>
      
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-400">
        <span>Author: <strong class="text-white">Ibadan Solar Hub</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Market Data: <strong class="text-white">PMS @ ₦1,400/L • Band A @ ₦209.50/kWh</strong></span>
        <span>•</span>
        <span>Updated: <strong class="text-white">September 2026</strong></span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-10 md:py-14">
    
    {/* Executive Summary Card */}
    <div class="bg-amber-500/10 border-2 border-solar-500/30 rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-950 flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="font-normal inline-block not-italic" aria-hidden="true">⚡</span> Executive Key Finding (Updated for Current Fuel Rates)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-800 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        With petrol at <strong>₦1,395 – ₦1,450/L</strong>, a standard Nigerian household (2 to 4-bedroom home) running a generator for just 5 to 7 hours daily burns between <strong>₦250,000 and ₦650,000 every month</strong> on fuel alone. When combined with Band A grid tariffs, total monthly power expenditure reaches <strong>₦325,000 to ₦800,000+</strong>. 
        <br><br>
        Because fuel costs have skyrocketed, an engineered <strong>2.5kVA – 5kVA Lithium (LiFePO4) solar installation now fully pays for itself in just 5.7 to 7.5 months</strong>. Over a 10-year LiFePO4 lifespan, solar saves between <strong>₦17 Million and ₦43 Million</strong> in direct cash.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Section 1: The Side-by-Side Comparison Table */}
    <div class="prose max-w-none mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">
        1. Side-by-Side Financial Comparison Table (PMS @ ₦1,400/L Baseline)
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Below is the updated empirical cost analysis across four realistic Nigerian household and office profiles using September 2026 market rates:
      </p>

      {/* Comparison Grid Table */}
      <div class="overflow-x-auto shadow-sm rounded-xl border border-slate-200 mb-8">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs sm:text-sm border-collapse bg-white">
          <thead class="bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Household Profile</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Monthly Band A Bill</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Monthly Fuel Bill (Gen @ ₦1,400/L)</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Total Monthly Power Burn</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">Turnkey Solar Setup</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800 bg-solar-600 text-slate-950">Payback Breakeven</th>
              <th class="p-3.5 border-b border-slate-800">5-Yr Net Savings</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-slate-700">
            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Starter / Remote Worker</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">1-2 Rooms, Laptops, Starlink, Fans, TV</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦31,500 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(150 kWh)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦94,500 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(3 hrs/day Small Gen • 2.25L/day)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦126,000/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦950,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(1.2kVA + 1.28kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">7.5 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦6,610,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition bg-amber-50/30">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Essential Home</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">2-3 Bed Flat, Inverter Fridge, TV, Fans</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦73,500 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(350 kWh)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦252,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(5 hrs/day 3.5kVA Gen • 6L/day)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦325,500/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦2,150,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(2.5kVA + 2.56kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">6.6 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦17,380,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Standard Comfort (Deep Freezer)</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">3-Bed Duplex, Freezer, Fridge, Water Dispenser</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦94,500 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(450 kWh)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦403,200 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(6 hrs/day 5kVA Gen • 9.6L/day)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦497,700/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦3,100,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(3.5kVA + 5.12kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">6.2 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦26,762,000</td>
            </tr>

            <tr class="hover:bg-slate-50 transition bg-solar-50/40">
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">
                <strong>Whole-Home + Inverter AC</strong><br>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-500 font-normal">4-Bed Duplex, 1.5HP AC, Pump, Deep Freezer</span>
              </td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦157,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(750 kWh)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5">₦646,800 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(7 hrs/day 7.5kVA Gen • 15.4L/day)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-red-600">₦803,800/mo</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-semibold text-slate-900">₦4,600,000 <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-400 block">(5kVA + 10.24kWh LiFePO4)</span></td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-extrabold text-green-700 bg-emerald-50">5.7 Months</td>
              <td class="p-3.5 font-bold text-slate-900">₦43,628,000</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 2: Why Band A is not 24/7 Independence */}
    <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900">
        2. The "Band A Illusion" vs. Real Grid Performance in Nigeria
      </h2>
      <p class="text-slate-700 text-sm md:text-base leading-relaxed">
        Many consumers initially believed paying <strong>₦209.50/kWh</strong> under Band A would guarantee uninterrupted power. However, field reports across IBEDC, EKEDC, IKEDC, AEDC, and EEDC demonstrate three ongoing points of failure:
      </p>
      
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 pt-2">
        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">⚡ National Grid System Collapses</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            When the transmission grid collapses, Band A feeders drop immediately to 0 Volts. Customers are forced back to their generators at ₦1,400/litre.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">🌧️ Localized Substation & Transformer Faults</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Fallen poles during storms, burnt feeder cables, and blown transformer fuses frequently cause multi-day blackouts in Band A estates.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-50 p-4 rounded-xl border border-slate-200">
          <div class="text-amber-600 font-bold text-sm mb-1">📈 Endless Tariff Inflation</div>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            DISCO tariffs adjust upward as the exchange rate and inflation shift. With Solar, your energy generation equipment is owned outright with 0 ongoing fuel cost.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 3: The 3 Cost Mistakes Nigerian Buyers Make */}
    <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 md:p-8 mb-12 space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold text-solar-400">
        3. The Three Cost Calculation Traps To Avoid
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-4 text-sm text-slate-300">
        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Trap #1: Ignoring Generator Maintenance & Oil Burn</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            Beyond ₦1,400/L petrol, running a generator requires engine oil changes (₦4,500 – ₦6,000 every 100 operating hours), replacement spark plugs, carburetors, and technician labor—adding ₦30,000 to ₦60,000 monthly to your real energy cost.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Trap #2: Buying Cheap Tubular Batteries Instead of Lithium (LiFePO4)</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            Tubular lead-acid batteries only offer 50% usable capacity (Depth of Discharge) and degrade within 2 to 3 years in Nigeria's tropical climate. High-grade LiFePO4 Lithium batteries deliver 80%–90% usable energy, last 10+ years (4,000+ cycles), and charge in just 2.5 hours of sunlight.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="border-l-4 border-solar-500 pl-4 py-1">
          <strong class="text-white">Trap #3: Skimping on Solar Panels</strong>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1">
            If you install a 5kVA inverter with only 2 or 4 panels, your battery will rarely reach 100% state-of-charge, forcing you to use generator power to charge batteries. Size panels to produce 1.25x your daily energy target.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 4: Interactive Calculator CTA */}
    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-solar-500 to-amber-400 rounded-2xl p-8 text-slate-950 mb-12 flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-black">Audit Your Load & Calculate Your Payback</h3>
        <p class="text-slate-900 text-sm mt-1 max-w-xl">
          Use our interactive 2026 Nigerian Solar Sizing Engine to select your exact appliances, compute required Inverter and Lithium battery specs, and export a 1-click printable BOQ specification sheet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a 
        href="/calculator"
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-950 hover:bg-slate-900 text-white font-bold px-6 py-3.5 rounded-xl shadow-lg transition transform active:scale-95 text-sm whitespace-nowrap"
      >
        <span>Open Solar Calculator</span>
        <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M14 5l7 7m0 0l-7 7m7-7H3" />
        </svg>
      </a>
    </div>

    {/* Section 5: Authoritative Digital Guides (Monetization) */}
    <div class="mb-14">
      <div class="text-center max-w-2xl mx-auto mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-slate-900">
          Official Nigerian Solar Publications
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-slate-600 mt-1">
          Authored & published by <strong>Ibadan Solar Hub</strong> to protect Nigerian buyers from overpaying or buying counterfeit solar equipment.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        {bookProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-amber-100 text-amber-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Flagship Ebook (30 Chapters)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{bookProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Author: {bookProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                {bookProduct.description}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Download</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={bookProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-solar-500 hover:bg-solar-600 text-slate-950 font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Buy on Selar (₦{bookProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}

        {toolkitProduct && (
          <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-6 shadow-sm flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div>
              <div class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-blue-100 text-blue-900 rounded-md text-xs font-bold mb-3">
                Complete Tool Bundle (4-in-1)
              </div>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">{toolkitProduct.title}</h3>
              <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 mt-1">Publisher: {toolkitProduct.author}</p>
              <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mt-3 leading-relaxed">
                {toolkitProduct.description}
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="mt-6 pt-4 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between">
              <div>
                <span class="text-xs text-slate-400 block">Instant Excel & PDF Bundle</span>
                <span class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900">₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()}</span>
              </div>
              <a
                href={toolkitProduct.checkoutUrl}
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 bg-slate-900 hover:bg-slate-800 text-white font-bold px-4 py-2.5 rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition"
              >
                Get Toolkit (₦{toolkitProduct.priceNgn.toLocaleString()})
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>
        )}
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Related Research Whitepapers Cross-Linking */}
    <div class="mb-14 bg-slate-50 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
        <span>📚</span> Related Nigerian Energy Research Whitepapers
      </h3>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-xs sm:text-sm">
        <a href="/nigeria-battery-lifespan-tco-study" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">Nigerian Battery Lifespan & 10-Yr TCO Study</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">LiFePO4 vs AGM Dry Cell vs Tall Tubular heat degradation models.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/nigeria-grid-collapse-feeder-reliability-report" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">National Grid Collapse & Feeder Reliability Report</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">11-year TCN collapse data (162 incidents) and Band A delivery deficits.</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/nigeria-lcoe-solar-vs-fuel-cost-index" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">The 2026 Nigerian LCOE Cost per kWh Index</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">Empirical kWh cost: Solar (₦150) vs CNG (₦315) vs Petrol (₦852).</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/nigeria-solar-radiation-yield-index" class="p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-slate-200 hover:border-solar-400 transition">
          <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 mb-1">The 36-State Solar Radiation & PV Yield Benchmark</div>
          <div class="text-slate-500">World Bank GIS radiation benchmarks from Sokoto to Port Harcourt.</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    {/* Section 6: Professional Social Sharing Bar */}
    <div class="bg-slate-900 text-white rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-slate-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
      <div>
        <span class="text-xs font-bold text-solar-400 uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">Knowledge is Power</span>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white">Share This Energy Cost Analysis</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-1 max-w-md">
          Help Nigerian homeowners, estate resident associations, and business owners calculate their true power costs and transition to reliable solar.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2.5 w-full sm:w-auto">
        <a
          href="https://api.whatsapp.com/send?text=Check%20out%20this%202026%20Nigerian%20energy%20cost%20analysis%20-%20Band%20A%20vs%20Petrol%20vs%20Solar%20Payback%20Index:%20https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 text-white font-bold rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition flex-1 sm:flex-initial"
        >
          <span>Share on WhatsApp</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold rounded-xl text-xs shadow transition flex-1 sm:flex-initial"
        >
          <span>Share on Facebook</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=The%202026%20Nigerian%20Power%20Index:%20Why%20running%20a%20generator%20at%20N1,400/L%20makes%20solar%20pay%20for%20itself%20in%20under%207%20months.&url=https://ibadansolarhub.com.ng/band-a-tariff-vs-solar-index"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 bg-slate-800 hover:bg-slate-700 text-slate-200 font-bold rounded-xl text-xs border border-slate-700 transition flex-1 sm:flex-initial"
        >
          <span>Post on X</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
